# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: clamps IOPS to 1 for a zero elapsed window or a zero-valued result")
expect(_iops(1000u64, 0u64)).to_equal(1u64)
expect(_iops(1u64, 1000000000u64)).to_equal(1u64)
```

</details>

#### keeps vfs_boot_init.spl importing the shared helpers instead of redefining them

- Verify: keeps vfs_boot_init.spl importing the shared helpers instead of redefining them
   - Expected: source contains `use os.services.vfs.q35_pure_nvme_perf_boot.{_elapsed_us, _iops}`
   - Expected: source does not contain `fn _vfs_boot_q35_elapsed_us(`
   - Expected: source does not contain `fn _vfs_boot_q35_iops(`
   - Expected: source contains `_elapsed_us(read_start, rt_time_now_unix_micros())`
   - Expected: source contains `_elapsed_us(write_start, rt_time_now_unix_micros())`
   - Expected: source contains `_iops(read_ops, read_total_us)`
   - Expected: source contains `_iops(write_ops, write_total_us)`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 10 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: keeps vfs_boot_init.spl importing the shared helpers instead of redefining them")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
val source = (read_file("src/os/services/vfs/vfs_boot_init.spl") + read_file("src/os/services/vfs/vfs_boot_core.spl") + read_file("src/os/services/vfs/vfs_boot_state.spl") + read_file("src/os/services/vfs/vfs_ambient_context.spl") + read_file("src/os/services/vfs/nvme_boot_runtime_owner.spl") + read_file("src/os/services/vfs/nvme_filesystem_direct_io.spl") + read_file("src/os/services/vfs/nvme_q35_lease_perf.spl") + read_file("src/os/services/vfs/direct_fat32_boot_reader.spl"))
expect(source.contains("use os.services.vfs.q35_pure_nvme_perf_boot.{_elapsed_us, _iops}")).to_equal(true)
expect(source.contains("fn _vfs_boot_q35_elapsed_us(")).to_equal(false)
expect(source.contains("fn _vfs_boot_q35_iops(")).to_equal(false)
expect(source.contains("_elapsed_us(read_start, rt_time_now_unix_micros())")).to_equal(true)
expect(source.contains("_elapsed_us(write_start, rt_time_now_unix_micros())")).to_equal(true)
expect(source.contains("_iops(read_ops, read_total_us)")).to_equal(true)
expect(source.contains("_iops(write_ops, write_total_us)")).to_equal(true)
```

</details>

